out.push(A('_(No Practise line in x.7. The Language box in a Review & Mediate cycle collects the three moves and carries no Practise item — the house pattern at every level of this series.)_'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the cycle in which the level\'s peer-review band is really taught, and the Student\'s Book sets a trap for the class on purpose.** **Both readers in the printed case have been taught by this method and both are wrong** — **one as a classmate, one as an editor** — **and the class will side with the second reader, because the second reader sounds like somebody who knows what they are doing.** **Let them, and then ask one question: _if she cuts sentences three and four, what will she be writing in June?_** **B2 paragraphs, two sentences shorter.** ⚠ **The deeper point is the one Mr Attar supplies from his own experience: a rule is kept and the paper is lost.** **He was given a rule in June and did nothing with it, and he is the only person in the room entitled to say so.** **Let him say it, do not soften it, and do not let the room reassure him** — **the eight newcomers are about to be given a book full of rules and they need to hear what happened to the last person who was handed one.**'));
