out.push(A('⚠ **Item 1 separates the class and is worth four minutes.** **_the delivery note read M16_ is a clause and would need _and_; _the delivery note reading M16_ is the construction.** **About a third of any room writes _read_**, because it sounds like English and is — a different sentence. **And item 5 is the one nobody expects to get wrong:** _let slip_ **takes the bare infinitive**, and _let slipped_ is produced by students who have correctly learned that the verb is in the past.'));
out.push(A('**B  Listening** **1** B   **2** A   **3** C   **4** B   **5** A   **6** C'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Listening Part 1 at C1 is three extracts with two questions each, and the difficulty is never the English — it is that the second question of a pair is about a different speaker from the first.** **Item 1 asks what the man says; item 2 asks what the woman is surprised by.** **Candidates answer both from the man.** **Teach the mechanical fix in Unit 1 and it is worth marks in every paper: before the recording starts, underline the person in each question.** ⚠ **And item 4 is the one to go over afterwards.** **Option A — _counsel objects to the translation_ — is explicitly denied in the recording** (_they do not object to my Arabic_), **and about half of any class chooses it, because the word _object_ is in the extract.** **A word from the recording attached to the wrong question is the commonest wrong answer in this part at every level.** **Say so once, here.**'));
